# Compile-time JavaScript templates are embedded verbatim by include_str!, so
# the bytes on disk become bytes in every generated project. Pin them to LF or
# a CRLF checkout would silently change generated output, differently per
# machine, where the original Rust "\n" escapes always emitted LF.
#
# Scoped to this directory deliberately. A blanket *.mjs rule would eventually
# renormalize runtime/*.mjs, which are emitted assets that already ship CRLF,
# and would change bytes those files have always written.
src/generate/templates/*.mjs text eol=lf
src/generate/templates/*.jsx text eol=lf
src/generate/templates/*.fragment text eol=lf
